ARCHITECTURE

This folder documents the system architecture of this repository's
project: the modules and how they connect, the data structures, the
algorithms, the dependencies, and the evaluations of other projects that
shaped them.


WHAT GOES HERE

  principles.md        the design rules every change follows
  data-structures.md   the main structures, as they are built today
  dependencies.md      every library the project uses, why, and which
                       version removes it
  <name>-evaluation.md how another project works; what to take from it
                       and what not to repeat

  A project without code yet starts with principles.md. Later phases add
  their own files; each plan says which.


KEEPING IT TRUE

  These documents describe the code as it is. A change that alters a
  structure, an algorithm or a dependency updates the matching file in
  the same commit. Where code and document disagree, the code is right
  and the document is a bug.


IN THIS REPOSITORY

  Architecture notes here document the patterns, data structures, and
  algorithms of the reference implementations tracked in ideas/, and how
  tam-ring plans to adapt them under the Tamlinux philosophy (pure C11,
  minimal dependencies, libtam-only linkage, and first-class Linux
  virtual console support).

  oama.md      architectural mechanisms and OAuth2 flows in oama
               (ideas/oama.md) and tam-ring's planned C11 adaptations
  pizauth.md   daemon vs. daemonless concurrency, locking, and token
               lifecycle in pizauth (ideas/pizauth.md) and tam-ring
